KZ3 patch 1111 (SPU pass 92): the lifted PPU's raw stores commit like vm_write* on a line an SPU has reserved.
From JonathanDC64/ps3recomp PR #38 (MIT; the Demon's Souls port), adapted: the fork fixed the SPU side, here the
store side is fixed.

The lifter writes stvx/stvxl, stvebx/stvehx/stvewx, stvlx/stvrx (+l), dcbz and stwbrx/sthbrx/stdbrx straight into
vm_base (VM_RAW_ST, vm_raw_st16, memset, a byte loop). Every other guest store goes through vm_write* (VM_WRITE_COH,
ppu_loader.cpp): on a reserved line it takes the line's stripe (patch 1056), writes, and calls
spu_coh_notify_write, which breaks the SPU reservation and raises SPU_EVENT_LR. The raw stores did none of it, so:
- a raw store between a PUTLLC's compare and its copy (both under the stripe, spu_channels.c MFC_PUTLLC_CMD) is
  written back over by the PUTLLC's 128 bytes: a lost PPU store, which Cell never does (the store either kills the
  reservation first, so the PUTLLC fails, or lands after the commit);
- an SPU waiting on the line for SPU_EVENT_LR learns of the store only from the RdEventStat snapshot poll
  (spu_resv_lost_poll; one poll late, and an A-B-A store is missed).
PR #38's own bug (a no-op PUTLLC decided from resv_valid alone, the fork's PR #17) is not in our tree: our PUTLLC
compares the line with the snapshot under the stripe.

Now VM_RAW_ST and vm_raw_st16 test spu_coh_is_reserved (one load of a bitmap bit, as vm_write* does) and on a
reserved line call ppu_st_coh (ppu_loader.cpp: VM_WRITE_COH, plus ppu_resv_break_store when PPU_RESV_STORE is on).
A stvx is one locked commit, not two halves. dcbz and stvlx/stvrx always call ppu_st_coh; their new branches sit at
the top of _translate_op, ahead of the old ones, because patch 2082 rewrites the old branches' lines (the old
branches are unreachable now; ppu_st_coh's VM_WRITE_COH carries 2082's page store note).
KZ3_RAWST_COH=0 = the old plain copy (runtime switch; the lifted code is the same).
Test: tools/spu/test_r92_rawst_coh.sh (fails without this patch).

--- a/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
+++ b/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
@@ -2021,6 +2021,25 @@
 {
     barrier_watch_hit(ea, val, width, ra);
 }
+/* KZ3 patch 1111 (from JonathanDC64/ps3recomp PR #38, adapted): the commit of the lifted raw stores (stvx,
+ * stvebx/ehx/ewx, stvlx/stvrx, dcbz, st*brx; see VM_RAW_ST in ppu_lifter.py). Bytes already in guest order, one
+ * 128-byte line at most. vm_write*'s commit: under the line's stripe with the SPU reservation broken and
+ * SPU_EVENT_LR raised when an SPU holds the line, then the page store note. KZ3_RAWST_COH=0: the old plain copy
+ * (no stripe, no reservation broken; the note stays). */
+extern "C" void ppu_st_coh(uint32_t ea, const void* src, uint32_t n)
+{
+    static int s_on = -1;
+    if (__builtin_expect(s_on < 0, 0)) { const char* e = getenv("KZ3_RAWST_COH"); s_on = !(e && e[0] == '0'); }
+    if (!s_on) {
+        memcpy(vm_base + ea, src, n);
+#ifdef VM_STORE_NOTE   /* patch 2082, applied after this one */
+        VM_STORE_NOTE(ea, n);
+#endif
+        return;
+    }
+    VM_WRITE_COH(ea, src, n);
+    if (g_resv_store_active > 0) ppu_resv_break_store(ea);
+}
 void vm_write8 (uint64_t a, uint8_t  v) { VM_WW((uint32_t)a, v, 1, __builtin_return_address(0));   /* patch 1080 */
     if (vm_oob((uint32_t)a,1) || vm_null_store((uint32_t)a, v, 1, __builtin_return_address(0))) return;
